/-!
# De-risk: declared arith host-role helpers pinned by TEMPLATE equality

Fourth column of the declared-envelope family (`dCtorBody` / `concatPinnedAt`
lower the TYPE section from declaration; this module lowers the arith helper
CODE bodies). The certificate DECLARES which function index carries the
`Int.add` / `Int.sub` / `Int.mul` host-role contract (the manifest
`hostRoleTable`) plus the handful of indices the helper bodies mention; the
wall SYNTHESIZES the canonical helper body from that declaration
(meaning -> bytes) and pins the real code-section bytes by EQUALITY. No byte
is scanned to discover a role; a wrong declaration fails the pin.

The helper bodies are generated by our compiler from fixed WAT templates
(`src/codegen/wasm_gc/builtins/bignum.rs`, `emit_aint_addsub` /
`emit_aint_mul` / `emit_aint_from_i64`), so the honest body is a pure
function of six declared single-byte indices:

* `carrier`   — the `$aint` struct type index (the Int carrier),
* `limb`      — the limb array type index the bignum path reads,
* `decompose` / `normalize` / `strip` / `umagCmp` — the four factored
  bignum sub-routine FUNCTION indices the helper bodies call.

Every other byte of each body is a literal fixed by the WAT template.
De-risk scope: single-byte-LEB regime (`checkArithHostParams`, all declared
indices < 64), matching the real fixtures (largest observed index 108 is
json's `umagCmp`; the check admits < 128 for function indices to cover it
while staying single-byte).
-/

namespace ArithTemplateDerisk

/-- The arith host roles the manifest `hostRoleTable` can declare. `box` is
    name-bound in the trusted path already; it is included here because its
    body is the smallest instance of the same template family. -/
inductive ArithRole where
  | box | add | sub | mul
deriving Repr, DecidableEq

/-- The DECLARED indices the helper bodies are a function of. Nothing here is
    computed from bytes: the producer declares them, the wall synthesizes. -/
structure ArithHostParams where
  carrier   : Nat
  limb      : Nat
  decompose : Nat
  normalize : Nat
  strip     : Nat
  umagCmp   : Nat
deriving Repr, DecidableEq

/-- Signed-LEB (`s33`) encoding of a heap-type index, fail-closed to at most two
    bytes. A concrete type index inside `ref null` is encoded as a signed LEB, so
    it needs two bytes once the index reaches 64 (whose low seven bits set the
    sign bit): `64` is `c0 00`, not the unsigned `40`. Values below 64 stay a
    single byte, so the honest single-byte templates for the in-regime fixtures
    are unchanged. The `checkArithHostParams` bound keeps `carrier < 128`, so the
    quotient is `0` and the second byte's sign bit is always clear (positive). -/
def s33 (v : Nat) : List Nat :=
  if v < 64 then [v]
  else [0x80 ||| (v % 128), (v / 128) % 64]

/-- LEB profile, fail-closed: the four sub-routine FUNCTION indices and the
    carrier encode within the template's holes. The limb array index stays a
    single byte in every position (< 64). The carrier is `< 128`: its unsigned
    `struct.new`/`struct.get` type-index positions stay one byte, while its
    signed `ref null` heap-type positions are lowered through `s33` (one byte
    below 64, two bytes at 64..127). -/
def checkArithHostParams (p : ArithHostParams) : Bool :=
  decide (p.carrier < 128) && decide (p.limb < 64) &&
  decide (p.decompose < 128) && decide (p.normalize < 128) &&
  decide (p.strip < 128) && decide (p.umagCmp < 128)

/-! ## Canonical byte LOWERING of each declared helper body (meaning -> bytes)

Each definition mirrors one WAT template: a fixed literal skeleton with the
declared indices spliced in at the template's parameter positions. -/

